# LINE ENDINGS ARE PINNED, ON EVERY PLATFORM.
#
# Without this file a Windows clone can end up with CRLF in the working tree
# while the index holds LF, and then EVERY tracked file reports as modified:
# measured on the operator's machine, 56 files, 10,661 insertions and 10,661
# deletions, and not one character of content different.
#
# Three things break, in rising order of seriousness:
#   1. `git status` is useless, so a real edit hides among 56 false ones.
#   2. `git merge --ff-only` refuses, and the next kit update cannot be pulled.
#   3. tests/SOURCE_SHA256.txt and tests/fixtures/manifest.json hash FILES. A
#      line ending is a byte. A manifest that disagrees with its own working
#      tree is FK-01 arriving by a different road.
#
# This kit is Python, Markdown and JSON. It has no file that wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything hashed by a manifest is byte-exact by definition. Say so explicitly
# rather than relying on `text=auto` guessing right.
tests/SOURCE_SHA256.txt   -text
tests/fixtures/manifest.json -text

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mov  binary
*.zip  binary
*.pdf  binary
